--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Scope notes (not a second licence — the grant above is the whole licence)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

**Artwork is included.** The MIT grant above covers the whole of this
repository, *including* the owner-supplied artwork: the art pack
(`public/assets/artpack/`), the panel frames (`public/assets/ui/frame-*.png`),
the inventory slot frame (`public/assets/ui/slot.png`), and the environment,
title and weapon sprites. The copyright holder confirmed on 2026-11-26 that
this artwork is **not** excluded from the grant.

**Third-party components keep their own licences.** Nothing here relicenses
them; each keeps the terms it shipped with, enumerated with its provenance in
`THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`:

| Component | Licence |
| --- | --- |
| Phaser 4 | MIT |
| Ark Pixel Font | SIL Open Font License 1.1 |
| Kenney "Pixel UI Pack" selection marker | CC0 1.0 |
| pixelfx effect sheets | MIT |

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Adoption record
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This file was a draft marked `STATUS — PENDING OWNER CONFIRMATION` until the
copyright holder adopted it on **2026-11-26**, deciding three things:

1. MIT is the licence; the copyright holder is **Zhuyuyangyy** (repository
   owner, and the ModelScope account that hosts the deployed Studio).
2. The scope is **not** code-only — the owner's artwork is covered by the same
   MIT grant.
3. Third-party components keep their own licences, listed individually rather
   than as a blanket disclaimer.

The draft's text and its reasoning are preserved in the git history
(`git log -- LICENSE`); a LICENSE file with two competing licences in it grants
nothing clearly, so the draft block was replaced rather than appended to.
